message: "If you use Helionyx in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Helionyx: open-source hybrid renewable energy sizing for AI assistants"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jayath
    family-names: De Silva
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jayzilva/helionyx"
url: "https://github.com/Jayzilva/helionyx"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - hybrid renewable energy
  - microgrid sizing
  - solar PV
  - battery storage
  - techno-economic analysis
  - Sri Lanka
abstract: >-
  Helionyx is a Model Context Protocol server, command-line interface and Claude skill
  that sizes hybrid energy systems (solar PV, wind, battery, diesel generator and grid).
  It simulates every candidate design hour by hour for a year, discards designs that break
  constraints and ranks the rest by net present cost, so an AI assistant can explain
  results that come from a deterministic, reproducible solver run.
